Screen protector samples circulating online offer an early look at how Apple's rumored iPhone 20 Pro redesign could look, with rounded edges that could help create the appearance of a nearly borderless display.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/iphone-20-pro-screen-protectors.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077875" /><br/>
Sharing a video of the purported screen protector on <a href="https://x.com/UniverseIce/status/2122317049716503012">X yesterday</a>, the leaker known as "Ice Universe" described next year's anticipated iPhone redesign as a "milestone." In a <a href="https://weibo.com/5673255066/5366200859363121">follow-up post</a> on Weibo today, Ice Universe added, in translation, that "the era of easy screen protector application is coming to an end. The era of a comfortable grip is approaching."<br/>
<br/>
The glass illustrates several elements repeatedly described in rumors about the anniversary iPhone, including shallow curves along all four edges, rounded corners, and an extremely narrow border.<br/>
