The post follows a separate handheld video shared by Ice Universe on November 14, with text identifying it as an approved "3D quad-curved cover glass" sample. Similar glass pieces have been circulating since early October on Weibo and X. On <a href="https://weibo.com/2/detail/5351442713936669">October 7</a>, Weibo blogger "体验more" shared photographs of samples in two sizes, suggesting that they looked like concept designs based on leaked information.<br/>
<br/>
The screen protectors likely represent early manufacturing tests based on rumors, rather than parts made to Apple's actual specifications. Experimental pieces allow manufacturers to explore new manufacturing techniques ahead of having access to the finished device's dimensions.<br/>
<br/>
The samples also show a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a> that appears comparable to the narrower version introduced on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a>. That would suggest no further substantial reduction for the anniversary model, in line with display analyst Ross Young's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/22/20TH-ANNIVERSARY-IPHONE-ALL-SCREEN-DESIGN-IN-DOUBT/">prediction</a> that the smaller &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj; would remain through 2027.<br/>
<br/>
The glass offers a physical depiction of the design direction described in earlier rumors. Ice Universe previously suggested that the anniversary iPhone would use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/28/20th-anniversary-iphone-liquid-glass-display/">shallow curves</a> alongside optical refraction and other visual effects to make the display borders less visible. <br/>
<br/>
That shape could also complicate screen protector designs. A protector covering the curved edges would need to follow their contours closely, making its fit dependent on the final glass geometry. Ice Universe's latest comments point to that potential tradeoff between a more rounded feel and the convenience of applying a flat protector.<br/>
<br/>
The footage arrives amid an increasingly detailed picture of the 20th anniversary iPhone. Yesterday, the leaker "Fixed Focus Digital" claimed that the models would use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-20-pro-to-be-based-on-iphone-air/">glass similar to the iPhone Air</a>, but with greater curvature on all four sides. Apple's 20th-anniversary iPhone models are expected in the fall of 2027, although the "iPhone 20 Pro" name remains speculative.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/20th-anniversary-iphone/">20th-Anniversary iPhone</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ice-universe/">Ice Universe</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/iphone-20-pro-screen-protectors-rumored-design/">iPhone 20 Pro Screen Protectors Show Rumored Curved Design</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-20-pro-screen-protectors-show-rumored-curved-design.2494643/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>